  "notes": "Roots-rock-informed adult pop over loop-based grooves: 76–128 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the signature mid-tempos at 95–121. The feel is the entry's clearest claim and it is authored twice over — \"kick 1 and 3 with a swung 16th push\" gives `swing` 0.56 on a 16th grid, and \"snare 2&4 slightly behind the grid\" gives `offGridMs` 9, the only positive snare offset in this batch. The third delta is \"tambourine or shaker on 8ths\" with \"brush and rimshot textures on the ballads\", which is the tambourine/shaker/rim perc block. Harmony is major and blues-inflected — I–IV–V with a flat-7 mixolydian colour, and I–vi–IV–V for the ballads — so mixolydian carries real weight in the scales. The bass is \"a rounded pick attack, root-and-fifth motion, walking passing notes into changes\", which is `independent_riff` at 0.7 with the widest passing-tone set here. The melody \"sits in a narrow low-alto band with conversational phrasing and a repeated hook cell\", i.e. a low, narrow register with a `riff_loop` structure. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says so: tempo anchors are sourced, the harmonic and drum specifics are convention-derived, and the tempo values are catalogue readings across mixed eras. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are `swing.amount`, `offGridMs` and every drum probability.",
